      "content": "Gnomes? That's a very specific comparison. It's a bit of a strange thing to say in a professional context, but I guess I see what you mean about the energy of it—that sense of chaotic, tiny, pointless movement. \n\nIt's just so unsettling. It feels less like a \"nuisance\" and more like there's something actually *there* in the room with us, something small that's just enjoying the chaos it's making. It's making the whole crew really jumpy. \n\nCan we get back to that tracking method you mentioned? How exactly do we document these \"patterns\" without making the team look paranoid or losing focus on the actual medical symposium? I want to stay professional, but I also need to keep everyone from losing their minds.",
